From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fork contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ios: edit the touch controls from the in-game menu (move,
 per-button size up to 400%, opacity, custom macros)

Adds an upgraded Edit control layout editor to the in-game menu (GameMenu.swift). It opens a
collapsible floating editor card over the game supporting:
- Global and per-button resizing from 40% to 400% (tap any control or custom macro to resize it
  individually, tap the percentage to snap back to 100%, or use All Size for every control).
- Smooth free drag positioning inside the screen/controls bounds with Split ABXY support to
  resize and position A, B, X and Y individually, plus overlap-aware selection and guaranteed
  menu gear reachability.
- Custom multi-button macro buttons (up to 12 per layout set) with a 4x4 Switch button picker
  (e.g. X+A), Hold / Toggle / Turbo modes, optional custom label with live preview, and
  per-macro resizing (40% to 400%) and dragging.
- Opacity control (15% to 100%), per-item Reset, a two-option Reset menu (keep or clear macros),
  Cancel and Done.

Done saves layout arrangement, global scale, per-control custom scales/positions, custom macros
and opacity in NSUserDefaults, so a game's own app keeps them across launches. Saved layout/size
edits drop when DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT or DM_TOUCH_SIZE in the environment changes, while custom macros
are preserved.

DmPadGeometry.h gains DmPadCustom, DmPadMacro/DmPadMacros, dm_pad_apply_custom and encode/parse/
hit-testing helpers, covered across all 14 screens in pad_geometry_check.m.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Let a game's own app (no launcher) edit the touch controls in game: move, per-button size up to 400%, opacity, and custom multi-button macro buttons
Issue: none
